# Reusable stats panel and unit-card popover plan

This checklist is the implementation source of truth for the following open
item in `docs/project.todo`:

> Add a SoulSearch "stats view" modal-window popover to the base game's unit
> card window, so users can inspect a unit without opening the full SoulSearch
> window.

The work has two inseparable parts:

1. encapsulate the existing Stats panel as a behavior-complete reusable
   component; and
2. use that component in a new popover opened from a DFHack overlay button on
   the vanilla unit card.

Do not mark the parent `docs/project.todo` item complete until every automated
gate and the final live fortress-mode gate in this document has passed.

Record phase results in the `Execution evidence` table at the end of this
document. Every completed phase gate must have a dated entry that identifies
the commands, tests, screenshots/observations, or live fortress checks that
justify marking it complete.

## Target behavior

- [ ] The main SoulSearch window and the unit-card popover instantiate the same
      reusable Stats component.
- [ ] The shared component owns its views, relative layout, rendered records,
      scrolling behavior, sort interaction, hit-testing, and stats tooltips.
- [ ] The main window preserves its current Stats geometry and interaction
      behavior. The only planned copy change is replacing resident-specific
      empty/fallback Stats wording with the generic term `unit` for both hosts.
- [ ] A visible SoulSearch button appears only in the confirmed vanilla
      fortress-mode unit-card focus context or context set (expected root:
      `dwarfmode/ViewSheets/UNIT`).
- [ ] Activating the button captures the unit currently displayed by the
      vanilla card and opens a compact modal Stats popover for that unit.
- [ ] The popover is a centered, non-draggable, non-resizable, non-persisted
      singleton. Repeated activation must not create stacked copies, and a
      valid activation for a different unit must update that singleton to the
      newly captured unit and reset its sort and scroll state. Re-activation
      for the same unit retains that state.
- [ ] The popover does not open the results list, filter editor, presets, or any
      other part of the full SoulSearch window.
- [ ] Closing the popover returns the player to the same vanilla unit card.

## Architectural constraints

- [ ] Add functionality through DFHack's overlay framework; do not modify or
      retain references to the vanilla unit card's internal widget tree.
- [ ] Capture the selected `df.unit` before showing the new
      `gui.ZScreenModal`.
      Selection lookup must not depend on the popover already being on top.
- [ ] Snapshot only the selected unit when opening the popover. Validate and
      collect that unit before showing a screen; do not collect or search every
      fortress candidate for a single-unit stats view.
- [ ] Keep `stats_presenter.lua` responsible for presentation records and
      formatted content; do not duplicate attribute evaluation or formatting
      in the popover.
- [ ] Define a narrow `SoulSearchStatsSubject` data contract for Stats hosts:
      `unit`, `unit_id`, `row`, `name`, `profession`, and `filter_criteria`.
      Normal search results must satisfy it structurally, and singleton identity
      comparisons must use the stable `unit_id` snapshot.
- [ ] Use the generic term `unit` in shared Stats empty and fallback copy. Do
      not add host-supplied terminology or display options to the subject or
      public popover API.
- [ ] Keep unit collection and Stats-subject construction separate:
  - [ ] `residents.collect_unit(unit)` returns
        `SoulSearchResidentRow|nil, error|nil`;
  - [ ] `stats_subject.from_row(row, filter_criteria)` returns one
        `SoulSearchStatsSubject`; and
  - [ ] the popover composes those operations with an empty criteria sequence.
- [ ] Keep error reporting at the outer activation boundary. Collection and
      popover APIs return errors without printing; mouse/CLI activation reports
      the final error exactly once. After a screen has been shown, its
      `onResize()` lifecycle path is the sole exception: it may report one
      unsupported-size error immediately before dismissing itself.
- [ ] Update `stats_presenter.lua` APIs and LuaDoc to consume
      `SoulSearchStatsSubject`, not the wider search-result contract.
- [ ] Keep reusable column dimensions and hitbox boundaries in a dependency-
      free `stats_layout.lua`. `ui_format.lua` and `stats_panel.lua` may both
      consume it; neither may import the other.
- [ ] Keep Stats sort validation, defaults, and next-state transitions in a
      pure `stats_sort.lua` module shared by all Stats hosts. Do not move or
      change result-list sort behavior as part of this extraction.
- [ ] Keep sort persistence outside the reusable component. The component may
      own active sort interaction state, but reports changes through a callback
      so each host decides whether and where to save them.
- [ ] Treat programmatic `set_sort(sort)` as silent. Invoke
      `on_sort_change(sort)` only for a user-initiated sort transition, avoiding
      persistence callbacks during initialization or host refresh.
- [ ] Keep main-window settings and popover settings independent. Opening or
      sorting the popover must not silently mutate the default SoulSearch
      window's saved settings.
- [ ] Keep tooltip rendering at screen level so it can escape panel clipping.
      The reusable Stats component should expose its current tooltip text to
      either host screen.
- [ ] Extract the screen-level tooltip renderer into `ui_tooltip.lua` with a
      host-agnostic `get_tooltip_text() -> string` owner contract. Use an empty
      string, not `nil`, when no tooltip is active.
- [ ] Register every new internal module in `module_registry.lua` and in the
      pure-Lua test harness where required.
- [ ] Register every SoulSearch-owned popover screen with `screen_registry.lua`
      so `soulsearch reload` and teardown dismiss it safely.
- [ ] Make popover registration and dismissal idempotent across explicit close,
      `onDismiss`, `onDestroy`, reload, and invalid-unit failure paths.
- [ ] Do not let the overlay widget retain a stale local reference to a
      reloadable popover module. Resolve the popover entry point dynamically on
      activation, and make `soulsearch reload` rescan/reconstruct the overlay
      widget before reuse.
- [ ] Clear the overlay registration script's DFHack script environment before
      production rescan so removed globals and class methods cannot survive a
      reload.

## Phase 0 - Baseline and vanilla integration proof

- [ ] Record the current main-window Stats behavior before refactoring:
  - [ ] title, underline, unit name, profession, and selected-filter summary;
  - [ ] physical, mental, and trait color categories;
  - [ ] omission of stats that do not deviate meaningfully from baseline;
  - [ ] fixed `Stat` and `Delta` header with independently scrolling rows;
  - [ ] stat-name and delta sort cycles and their current default directions;
  - [ ] stat-name, sort-header, and delta tooltips;
  - [ ] correct tooltip record after scrolling via `start_line_num`;
  - [ ] whether subject changes and sort changes reset or retain scroll;
  - [ ] keyboard focus/traversal order around the Stats views; and
  - [ ] empty/no-selection behavior.
- [ ] In a current fortress, verify and record the vanilla unit-card focus
      string or set of strings with `dfhack.gui.getFocusStrings()` for every
      practical entry route.
- [ ] Verify `dfhack.gui.getSelectedUnit(true)` returns the unit displayed on
      `dwarfmode/ViewSheets/UNIT` before any SoulSearch screen is shown.
- [ ] Verify a module-loadable script under `scripts_modinstalled` can register
      an `OVERLAY_WIDGETS` entry and constrain it to the unit-card focus path.
- [ ] Verify `gui.ZScreenModal` pauses and blocks input as expected when opened
      from both paused and unpaused unit cards, and record the intended pause
      restoration behavior after dismissal.
- [ ] Record a safe default overlay-button position at the supported UI scales.
- [ ] Record an exact minimum supported width and height in DFHack tile-grid
      units returned by `dfhack.screen.getWindowSize()`, derived from the Stats
      columns, borders, close control, and at least one body row. Record pixel
      resolution and UI scale separately as evidence. Below the tile-grid
      minimum, the popover must refuse to open with a concise error instead of
      claiming to provide a usable clipped layout.
- [ ] Run the existing automated baseline before source changes:
  - [ ] `tools/Build.ps1`;
  - [ ] `tools/Test.ps1`; and
  - [ ] `git diff --check`.

### Phase 0 gate

- [ ] The unit-card focus, selected-unit lookup, overlay discovery, default
      placement, and current Stats behavior are evidence-backed rather than
      assumed.
- [ ] Existing automated gates are green before the extraction begins.

## Phase 1 - Characterize the reusable behavior seam

- [ ] Expand characterization coverage for all behavior moving out of
      `ui.lua`, `ui_components.lua`, and `ui_layout.lua`:
  - [ ] view composition and stable child IDs;
  - [ ] dynamic header/columns/body layout;
  - [ ] label and delta column boundaries;
  - [ ] the three-state sort cycle for both columns;
  - [ ] sort defaults and reverse-direction rules;
  - [ ] display-record retention, including section gaps;
  - [ ] header, delta, and attribute tooltip selection;
  - [ ] scrolled-row tooltip indexing;
  - [ ] scroll reset/retention on subject and sort changes;
  - [ ] current keyboard focus order and which inputs reach the Stats area;
  - [ ] current layout refresh timing during main-window resize; and
  - [ ] current persistence behavior: user sort clicks update settings while
        initialization and ordinary Stats refresh do not.
- [ ] Characterize the existing one-unit data path with
      `residents.collect_units({unit})[1]` so the later
      `residents.collect_unit(unit)` adapter preserves the same row semantics
      without scanning a candidate scope.
- [ ] Add tests for units with:
  - [ ] physical, mental, and personality data;
  - [ ] no current soul;
  - [ ] no meaningful deviations; and
  - [ ] missing or fallback display names.
- [ ] Define and document the `SoulSearchStatsSubject` contract, including an
      stable `unit_id` snapshot, an empty `filter_criteria` sequence for
      unit-card subjects, and structural compatibility with normal SoulSearch
      results.
- [ ] Add characterization tests for the current resident-specific empty and
      fallback strings, then deliberately update the shared expectations from
      `No resident selected.` and `Unknown resident` to `No unit selected.` and
      `Unknown unit`. Record this as an intentional cross-host copy correction,
      not an extraction regression.
- [ ] Retain `SoulSearchResidentRow` as the historical internal row-type name
      and explicitly document that its structure supports any compatible
      `df.unit`. Do not introduce a cross-module row-type rename as part of this
      extraction.
- [ ] Enumerate the current Stats sort default, normalization, and transition
      cases in characterization tests without moving their implementation yet.
      Keep result-list sort cases separate.

### Phase 1 gate

- [ ] Tests fail if the extraction changes existing sort, hitbox, tooltip,
      scrolling, formatting, or empty-state behavior, except for the explicitly
      documented generic-unit copy correction.
- [ ] A one-unit row and structurally valid Stats subject can be constructed in
      tests without running a full search, while production ownership remains
      unchanged until Phase 2.

## Phase 2 - Extract the reusable Stats component

- [ ] Add a focused internal module, preferably `stats_panel.lua`, containing a
      `widgets.Panel`-derived reusable component.
- [ ] Add `stats_subject.lua` with a pure `from_row()` constructor and the
      canonical `SoulSearchStatsSubject` LuaDoc contract.
- [ ] Add `residents.collect_unit(unit)` as a one-row collection adapter that
      returns `row|nil, error|nil` and does not know about Stats subjects or
      presentation fields.
- [ ] Add dependency-free `stats_layout.lua` before moving layout constants:
  - [ ] move reusable label width, value-column position, and hitbox boundaries
        into it;
  - [ ] update `ui_format.lua` to consume it; and
  - [ ] keep main-window placement coordinates in `ui_layout.lua`.
- [ ] Add pure `stats_sort.lua` and make the component, Stats portion of window
      configuration, and tests consume its default, normalization, and
      next-state helpers. Leave result-list sort normalization in
      `window_config.lua`.
- [ ] Extract `SoulSearchTooltip` into `ui_tooltip.lua` without importing
      `ui.lua` or depending on `SoulSearchWindow`.
- [ ] Give the component a small host-facing API:
  - [ ] initial `subject` and `sort` attributes;
  - [ ] `set_subject(subject)`;
  - [ ] `set_sort(sort)`;
  - [ ] `reset_view_state(sort)`, which silently applies the supplied normalized
        sort and resets the scrollable body to its first row;
  - [ ] `get_sort()`;
  - [ ] `get_tooltip_text()`; and
  - [ ] `on_sort_change(sort)` callback.
- [ ] Add component-contract tests proving `set_sort()` is silent, user sort
      actions invoke `on_sort_change()`, `reset_view_state()` resets sort and
      scroll without invoking the callback, and relayout after a frame change
      does not require `set_subject()`.
- [ ] Move Stats-owned view creation into the component:
  - [ ] title and underline;
  - [ ] unit header;
  - [ ] fixed column header; and
  - [ ] scrollable stats body.
- [ ] Convert Stats layout from main-window absolute coordinates to
      component-relative coordinates.
- [ ] Recompute component-relative frames and hitboxes when the component's
      current `frame_body` changes through its layout lifecycle, independently
      of data refresh.
- [ ] If the component overrides `updateLayout()`, call the superclass layout
      implementation before applying component-relative dynamic frames.
- [ ] After changing the header, columns, or body frame, call each affected
      child's `updateLayout(frame_body)` with the component's current body
      rectangle, following the existing Stats relayout convention. Do not
      recursively re-enter the component's own `updateLayout()`.
- [ ] Export the component's minimum content dimensions from `stats_layout.lua`
      and test them against the recorded minimum supported tile-grid size.
- [ ] Preserve the current text column geometry and click boundaries unless a
      separately recorded live incompatibility requires a deliberate change.
- [ ] Move Stats-owned behavior into the component:
  - [ ] presentation refresh and `stats_records` retention;
  - [ ] sort-column hit-testing and sort cycling;
  - [ ] attribute-row and delta-cell hit-testing; and
  - [ ] header, attribute, and delta tooltip selection.
- [ ] Continue using `stats_presenter.lua` as the sole component-facing facade
      for Stats text and display records, with `ui_format.lua` remaining the
      underlying text formatter.
- [ ] Keep screen-sized tooltip positioning and painting outside the component.
- [ ] Remove obsolete Stats construction/update helpers from
      `ui_components.lua` after both behavior and tests have moved.
- [ ] Move component-internal constants and hit-testing out of the main-window
      `ui_layout.lua`; keep only the component's placement frame there and put
      shared formatting geometry in `stats_layout.lua`.
- [ ] Register every module introduced in this phase and update
      `tests/run.lua`, loader stubs, focused suites, and loader-contract tests
      in this phase rather than deferring them to Phase 6.
- [ ] Assert dependency-safe registry order explicitly:
  - [ ] `stats_layout` precedes `ui_format`;
  - [ ] `ui_format` precedes `stats_presenter`;
  - [ ] `ui_format` precedes `ui_tooltip` because tooltip wrapping consumes
        `ui_format.wrap_text()`;
  - [ ] `stats_sort` precedes `window_config` and `stats_panel`;
  - [ ] `stats_subject` precedes popover consumers;
  - [ ] `ui_tooltip` precedes `ui` and the popover screen; and
  - [ ] `stats_presenter`, `attribute_descriptions`, and `stats_layout` precede
        `stats_panel`, which precedes `ui`.

### Phase 2 gate

- [ ] The component can be instantiated in an arbitrary parent frame without
      referring to `STATS_LEFT`, the main window, result-list subviews, or
      `window_settings`.
- [ ] Component tests cover rendering state, sorting, layout, scrolling, and
      tooltips without constructing the full SoulSearch screen.
- [ ] `tools/Build.ps1`, `tools/Test.ps1`, and `git diff --check` pass.

## Phase 3 - Migrate the main SoulSearch window

- [ ] Replace the existing five loose Stats views with one reusable Stats
      component positioned at the current Stats panel location.
- [ ] Keep the `ui_refresh.apply()` owner contract unchanged. Implement
      `SoulSearchWindow:refresh_stats(result)` as the adapter that delegates to
      `self.subviews.stats_panel:set_subject(result)`, preserving the existing
      dispatcher and controlled result-selection callback suppression.
- [ ] Initialize the component from the current window identity's saved
      `stats_sort` snapshot.
- [ ] Persist sort changes through the component callback using the existing
      window-settings path.
- [ ] Make the main tooltip aggregator ask the Stats component for Stats-owned
      tooltip text while preserving the priority of unrelated control,
      results, filter, and picker tooltips.
- [ ] Render the aggregated tooltip through the shared `ui_tooltip.lua`
      screen-level view.
- [ ] Remove superseded Stats fields and methods from `SoulSearchWindow`,
      including duplicated sort, hit-test, tooltip, and refresh ownership.
- [ ] Preserve the current Stats panel placement, width, height, divider,
      header behavior, and scroll extent at the default window size.
- [ ] Preserve live resizing behavior and refresh the component layout from its
      own current `frame_body`.
- [ ] Preserve the main window's keyboard focus/traversal order and ensure the
      nested Stats panel does not consume unrelated input.
- [ ] Preserve the Phase 0 scroll reset/retention behavior when selection or
      sort changes call `set_subject()` or `set_sort()`.

### Phase 3 gate

- [ ] No main-window Stats rendering or interaction path bypasses the reusable
      component.
- [ ] Existing tests pass with the full-window callers migrated.
- [ ] `tools/Build.ps1`, `tools/Test.ps1`, and `git diff --check` pass for the
      migrated main-window implementation.
- [ ] Live fortress smoke confirms unchanged main-window geometry, sorting,
      scrolling, hover text, selection refresh, resizing, and saved sort state.

## Phase 4 - Implement the single-unit Stats popover

- [ ] Add a dedicated popover module and `gui.ZScreenModal` implementation
      rather than invoking `ui.open()` for the full SoulSearch window.
- [ ] Define the popover view hierarchy explicitly:
  - [ ] `SoulSearchStatsPopoverScreen` is the `gui.ZScreenModal` owner;
  - [ ] its primary child is a centered `widgets.Window` with
        `draggable=false`, `resizable=false`, and `frame_style=gui.FRAME_BOLD`
        so the external modal frame carries the required DFHack signature;
  - [ ] the reusable Stats component and explicit close control are children of
        that window; and
  - [ ] the shared tooltip is a direct screen-level sibling so it can escape
        window and component clipping.
- [ ] Implement
      `stats_popover.open(unit) -> screen|nil, error|nil` as a
      validate-before-show boundary:
  - [ ] confirm the captured unit ID still resolves to the same live unit;
  - [ ] collect exactly one row with `residents.collect_unit(unit)` and
        propagate, but do not print, any error;
  - [ ] construct the subject with `stats_subject.from_row(row, {})`;
  - [ ] construct and show the modal only after those steps succeed; and
  - [ ] return `nil, error` without registry or viewscreen changes on failure.
- [ ] Instantiate the reusable Stats component as the popover window's content.
- [ ] Implement the target window policy: centered, non-draggable,
      non-resizable, non-persisted, and clamped within the screen.
- [ ] Give the popover a compact frame that satisfies the component minimum at
      the exact Phase 0 supported tile-grid size.
- [ ] Add dedicated `stats_popover_config.lua` for popover defaults, minimum
      tile-grid dimensions, centering, and screen-bound clamping. Do not reuse
      the main window's private 90x30 normalization contract.
- [ ] Re-run screen-frame normalization and component layout from the screen's
      `onResize(w, h)` path; dismiss with a concise error if a resize makes the
      tile grid smaller than the supported minimum. Report that lifecycle error
      exactly once before dismissal and restore the pre-modal pause state.
- [ ] Call the superclass `onResize(w, h)` implementation before applying
      popover-specific frame normalization and child layout.
- [ ] Use the shared component's existing `Stats` heading as the popover's one
      visible content title; leave the containing window's `frame_title` unset
      so it does not add a second title. Add an explicit close control that does
      not overlap the title or its hitbox at the minimum supported size, plus
      normal `Esc`/right-click dismissal.
- [ ] Rely on `gui.ZScreenModal` for modal input and pause behavior so clicks do
      not activate controls on the vanilla card underneath it.
- [ ] Do not override `SoulSearchStatsPopoverScreen:onInput()`. Put any custom
      input behavior in the window or its child views and rely on inherited
      `gui.ZScreenModal` handling for `Esc`, right click, focus, and input
      blocking.
- [ ] Implement `onGetSelectedUnit()` on the popover screen and return the
      currently displayed subject's unit. A different-unit singleton update
      must change this result together with the visible subject.
- [ ] Add a shared `ui_tooltip.lua` screen-level sibling driven by
      `stats_panel:get_tooltip_text()`.
- [ ] Define popover sort state as independent from the main window:
  - [ ] initialize every new popover as unsorted
        (`{key=nil, reverse=false, phase=0}`);
  - [ ] retain it while the same unit ID remains displayed;
  - [ ] reset it, along with scroll position, on every new popover instance and
        every valid different-unit singleton replacement through the
        component's `reset_view_state()` API;
  - [ ] do not write it to the default SoulSearch window identity.
- [ ] Enforce a unit-aware singleton popover policy after validating and
      constructing the requested subject:
  - [ ] if no popover exists, create and show one;
  - [ ] if the active popover already shows the same unit ID, raise and return
        it without resetting state;
  - [ ] if it shows a different unit, update the existing screen atomically,
        reset sort and scroll state, then raise and return it; and
  - [ ] if new-unit validation fails, leave the existing popover unchanged and
        return `nil, error`.
- [ ] Register and unregister the popover through `screen_registry.lua`.
- [ ] Route explicit close, `onDismiss`, and `onDestroy` through one idempotent
      cleanup path that unregisters the screen exactly once.
- [ ] Add pure-Lua tests for subject construction, stale-unit rejection,
      unsupported screen size, same-unit and different-unit singleton behavior,
      failed singleton replacement, default/reset sort and scroll state,
      stable `unit_id` identity, modal window composition and signed frame,
      inherited screen input ownership, `onGetSelectedUnit()`, callbacks, close
      behavior, one-time resize error reporting, pause restoration, and teardown
      bookkeeping where the harness can model them.
- [ ] Update `tests/run.lua`, module-registry ordering/contracts, and test
      support loaders for all Phase 4 modules before running this phase's gate.
- [ ] Assert that `stats_popover_config`, `residents`, `stats_subject`,
      `stats_panel`, `ui_tooltip`, and `screen_registry` all precede
      `stats_popover` in the reload registry.

### Phase 4 gate

- [ ] The popover renders through the same Stats component used by the main
      window and contains no copied Stats formatting, sort, hit-test, scrolling,
      or tooltip logic.
- [ ] The public popover API is `stats_popover.open(unit)`. It requires only the
      captured unit and does not depend on caller-supplied display options or a
      live `SoulSearchWindow`.
- [ ] `tools/Build.ps1`, `tools/Test.ps1`, and `git diff --check` pass for the
      popover implementation.

## Phase 5 - Add the vanilla unit-card overlay button

- [ ] Add a module-loadable overlay registration script with `--@ module=true`.
      Module loading may define the widget class and global `OVERLAY_WIDGETS`,
      but must not look up units, print, register screens, or show UI.
- [ ] Define a global `OVERLAY_WIDGETS` entry backed by
      `overlay.OverlayWidget`.
- [ ] Choose and document a stable `OVERLAY_WIDGETS` key/widget identity. Set
      its overlay configuration version deliberately, and increment it only
      when intentionally resetting saved placement/configuration is required.
- [ ] Record the stable script path, widget key, and exact registered name shown
      by `overlay list`; treat all three as compatibility-sensitive identity.
- [ ] Restrict `viewscreens` to the confirmed fortress-mode unit-card focus
      path or path set instead of all of `dwarfmode`.
- [ ] Make the overlay enabled by default for first-time SoulSearch users while
      allowing normal disable/reposition control through DFHack.
- [ ] Render a clearly branded, compact SoulSearch Stats button at the recorded
      safe default position.
- [ ] Implement one shared activation helper that calls
      `dfhack.gui.getSelectedUnit(true)` before showing a screen, calls
      `stats_popover.open(unit)`, reports any selection or popover error exactly
      once, and returns only the screen or `nil`.
- [ ] Define activation ownership explicitly:
  - [ ] render the button through static, non-input child content and perform an
        explicit widget-frame hit-test for `_MOUSE_L` in the overlay widget;
  - [ ] call the shared helper only when that hit-test is inside the rendered
        button rectangle;
  - [ ] mouse `onInput()` returns `true` only after consuming that button click
        and delegates all other input to its superclass;
  - [ ] `overlay_trigger()` calls the same helper and returns the shown screen
        for DFHack CLI/keybinding ownership; and
  - [ ] `screen_registry.lua` tracks both paths for SoulSearch reload teardown,
        without becoming a second input owner.
- [ ] Resolve the popover module with `reqscript()` at activation time, or use
      an equivalently reload-safe lookup, so `soulsearch reload` cannot leave
      the widget calling a stale module table.
- [ ] Ensure the overlay widget itself is never attached as a popover subview.
- [ ] Keep the button static and omit `overlay_onupdate()` unless live evidence
      proves it is necessary. Never perform per-tick unit scanning or Stats
      recomputation.
- [ ] Add registration, focus-path, default-state, activation, missing-unit,
      and exact button-hitbox tests with overlay/GUI stubs:
  - [ ] exercise every button edge and immediately outside each edge; and
  - [ ] prove right click, scrolling, and unrelated clicks pass through without
        opening a popover or consuming vanilla unit-card input.
- [ ] Update `tests/run.lua` and overlay/GUI test support in Phase 5 before
      running this phase's gate.
- [ ] Document the development reload procedure:
      `:lua require('plugins.overlay').rescan()` after script changes.
- [ ] Document that removing or renaming overlay-script globals during
      development additionally requires
      `devel/clear-script-env <overlay-script>` before the rescan.
- [ ] Define the production `soulsearch reload` behavior explicitly:
  - [ ] dismiss all registered main and popover screens;
  - [ ] capture the old registry's complete script-name list before clearing
        any environment;
  - [ ] clear every module environment in that old list except the registry so
        removed module entries cannot survive;
  - [ ] clear and run `internal/soulsearch/module_registry`, reacquire and
        validate the fresh registry table, and replace the command's cached
        coordinator reference;
  - [ ] clear every module named by the fresh registry's `MODULES` sequence,
        including newly added entries but not the newly loaded registry itself,
        then run that sequence in dependency order;
  - [ ] run `devel/clear-script-env` for the stable overlay registration script
        path without manually executing that script;
  - [ ] always call `require('plugins.overlay').rescan()` so overlay-class
        changes are refreshed as well as dynamic popover dependencies;
  - [ ] preserve the existing behavior of opening the main SoulSearch window
        after reload; and
  - [ ] prove that, after closing that window and returning to a unit card, the
        next button activation uses the current overlay and popover code.
- [ ] Add command-level reload tests that model an added module, a removed
      module, a reordered dependency, and a changed registry contract, proving
      the fresh registry generation rather than the cached pre-reload table
      controls reconstruction.

### Phase 5 gate

- [ ] `overlay list` discovers the widget and `gui/control-panel` can enable or
      disable it.
- [ ] The button appears on the vanilla unit card and nowhere outside its
      confirmed focus context.
- [ ] Activating it always opens Stats for the unit that was visible at click
      time.
- [ ] `tools/Build.ps1`, `tools/Test.ps1`, and `git diff --check` pass for the
      overlay and reload implementation.

## Phase 6 - Automated integration, packaging, and documentation

- [ ] Audit that each prior implementation phase updated `tests/run.lua`, the
      module registry, dependency-order contracts, and test support loaders at
      the time its new suites and modules were introduced. Fix any omissions
      before packaging.
- [ ] Update README/help text to describe:
  - [ ] the unit-card Stats button;
  - [ ] overlay enable/disable and reposition behavior; and
  - [ ] the relationship between the compact popover and full SoulSearch.
- [ ] Ensure the source and packaged mod contain the overlay registration and
      every runtime dependency.
- [ ] Add command-level coverage proving `soulsearch reload` dismisses all
      registered screens, replaces the cached registry coordinator, reconstructs
      modules from the fresh registry generation, clears the overlay script
      environment, requests an overlay rescan without manually executing the
      overlay script, and retains the existing main-window reopen behavior.
- [ ] Run the automated closure sequence separately:
  - [ ] `tools/Build.ps1`;
  - [ ] `tools/Test.ps1`;
  - [ ] `tools/Publish.ps1`;
  - [ ] `tools/VerifyPackage.ps1`; and
  - [ ] `git diff --check`.
- [ ] Record production Lua count, test count, package path, and all command
      results in this document when the phase is executed.

### Phase 6 gate

- [ ] Syntax, pure-Lua behavior, package contents, documentation, and whitespace
      checks are green.
- [ ] Automated success is not treated as proof of live overlay placement,
      focus, input, or rendering behavior.

## Phase 7 - Live fortress-mode acceptance

### Main-window regression

- [ ] Open the full SoulSearch window and confirm results selection still
      refreshes the shared Stats component.
- [ ] Confirm name, profession, selected-filter summary, colors, deviations,
      separators, and empty states match the Phase 0 baseline except for the
      documented generic-unit copy correction.
- [ ] Exercise all three states of both Stats sort headers.
- [ ] Scroll the Stats body and verify attribute tooltips continue to describe
      the row under the mouse, not the pre-scroll row.
- [ ] Verify the delta and header tooltips at both edges and immediately outside
      their hitboxes.
- [ ] Resize, drag, close, and reopen the full window; verify Stats layout and
      saved sort behavior remain intact.
- [ ] Verify subject and sort changes preserve the Phase 0 scroll policy and
      that keyboard focus/traversal remains unchanged after nesting the panel.

### Overlay and popover acceptance

- [ ] Confirm the overlay is listed, enabled by default on first registration,
      and configurable through `gui/control-panel` and `gui/overlay`.
- [ ] Open vanilla unit cards from every practical entry route and confirm the
      button appears consistently.
- [ ] Confirm the button does not appear on item sheets, the creatures list,
      the main map, or unrelated information tabs.
- [ ] Open the popover for several units and verify each captured identity,
      profession, attributes, traits, deviations, and colors are current.
- [ ] While each popover is active, verify DFHack selected-unit lookup returns
      the same unit through the popover's `onGetSelectedUnit()` implementation.
- [ ] Include at least:
  - [ ] a normal citizen with a current soul;
  - [ ] a non-citizen or visitor accessible from a unit card;
  - [ ] an animal or other unit without a current soul; and
  - [ ] a unit with few or no meaningful deviations.
- [ ] Exercise sorting, scrolling, stat-name tooltips, header tooltips, and
      delta tooltips in the popover.
- [ ] From a unit card, invoke `overlay trigger <registered-name>` and confirm
      the CLI path opens the same popover through `overlay_trigger()`.
- [ ] Click every edge of the rendered overlay button and immediately outside
      each edge; confirm only in-bounds left clicks open the popover and all
      unrelated input continues to reach the vanilla unit card.
- [ ] Close with the close control, `Esc`, and right click; confirm the same
      vanilla unit card is revealed and receives no accidental click-through.
- [ ] Reopen for a different unit and confirm no stale unit data or scroll
      position leaks into the new popover and sort returns to the documented
      unsorted default.
- [ ] Call `stats_popover.open(captured_unit)` again while the popover is open;
      confirm the existing singleton is returned or raised and no modal is
      stacked behind it.
- [ ] While the singleton is open, call `stats_popover.open(other_unit)` and
      confirm the same modal atomically switches identity, resets sort/scroll,
      and remains the only popover screen.
- [ ] Attempt that replacement with a stale/invalid unit and confirm the error
      is returned without printing while the existing valid subject remains
      unchanged.
- [ ] Verify the centered button-launched popover at the exact Phase 0 minimum
      DFHack tile-grid dimensions and at multiple pixel resolutions/UI scales;
      confirm its frame remains visible and all controls remain clickable.
- [ ] Verify a tile grid smaller than the supported minimum is rejected cleanly
      without adding a screen or registry entry. Resize an open popover below
      the minimum and confirm exactly one error is reported and dismissal and
      pause restoration are clean.
- [ ] Reposition and disable the overlay, restart/reload as appropriate, and
      confirm DFHack preserves the user's overlay configuration.
- [ ] Measure idle overlay cost over comparable unit-card intervals with the
      overlay enabled and disabled:
  - [ ] reset performance counters before each interval with
        `dfhack.internal.resetPerfCounters()` when the card can remain unpaused;
  - [ ] if the unit card forces pause, use
        `dfhack.internal.resetPerfCounters(true)` and label the result as
        all-elapsed-time rather than unpaused-gameplay evidence;
  - [ ] print each result with
        `require('script-manager').print_timers()`; and
  - [ ] record the registered overlay's timer contribution and confirm it is
        well below one percent of elapsed time, investigating any material or
        unstable result before claiming the button is inexpensive while idle.
- [ ] Run `soulsearch reload` with the main window and popover open in separate
      passes; confirm owned screens dismiss cleanly and the existing main
      SoulSearch window opens after reload. Close it, return to a unit card,
      and confirm the rescanned overlay opens the current popover implementation.
- [ ] Repeat popover open/close from both paused and unpaused unit cards;
      confirm modal input never leaks and dismissal restores the intended pause
      state.
- [ ] Leave the fortress/map while no popover is open and confirm no stale unit
      or screen state causes an error on the next valid use.

### Phase 7 gate

- [ ] Main-window behavior is preserved and the same Stats component is visibly
      operating in both hosts.
- [ ] Unit-card focus, selected-unit capture, overlay lifecycle, modal input,
      screen teardown, tooltip accuracy, constrained-window layout, and measured
      idle overlay cost all pass live validation.
- [ ] Mark the corresponding `docs/project.todo` item complete with the live
      validation date and update this checklist with the recorded evidence.

## Definition of done

- [ ] One reusable Stats component owns all shared Stats UI behavior.
- [ ] Both the full SoulSearch window and unit-card popover use it directly.
- [ ] The vanilla unit-card button is discoverable, focused to the correct
      context, configurable, and measured to be inexpensive while idle.
- [ ] Automated build, tests, package verification, and diff checks pass.
- [ ] The full live fortress-mode acceptance checklist passes.
- [ ] Documentation and `docs/project.todo` reflect the completed behavior.

